    <bpmn:process id="W_W4800" name="W4800. Network Expansion Governance, Capex Approval &amp; Portfolio Prioritization" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Phase rollout (W4793); annual capex cycle; performance review (W4815)
Frequency: Annual + per phase
Volume: 1 portfolio governance; ~phased capex
Owner: Locker Program Manager / PMO (VS-112) / Finance
Participants: PMO (VS-112), Capex (VS-40), Strategy (VS-33), Real Estate (VS-97)
Source: workflow W4800 — Network Expansion Governance, Capex Approval &amp; Portfolio Prioritization</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4800_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4800_Lane1" name="Locker Program">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4800_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4800_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4800_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4800_Lane2" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4800_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4800_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4800_Start4" name="Phase rollout (W4793); annual capex cycle; performance review (W4815)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4800_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4800_Task5" name="Maintain the locker-portfolio roadmap &amp; capex pipeline: candidate sites…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Maintain the locker-portfolio roadmap &amp; capex pipeline: candidate sites (W4795), phased rollout aligned to BOPIS growth (VS-10) and store-remodel/new-store (VS-109/VS-37), own-vs-partner mix, off-site vs in-store mix, and the multi-year capex envelope; integrate into the corporate capex plan (VS-40/VS-112)
Responsible (R): Locker Program / PMO / Finance
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc. / CFO
Duration: Annual + continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4800_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4800_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4800_Task6" name="Govern capex approval per the tiered matrix (VS-40): business case (W4793)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Govern capex approval per the tiered matrix (VS-40): business case (W4793), ROI/utilization thresholds, phase-gate review (deploy → measure pickup/returns/3P/footfall → decide next phase); escalate material capex to the board (VS-36)
Responsible (R): Finance / PMO / Strategy
Accountable (A): COO / CFO / Board
Duration: Per phase</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4800_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4800_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4800_Task7" name="Prioritize dynamically using performance data (W4815): reallocate capex from…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Prioritize dynamically using performance data (W4815): reallocate capex from under-performing to over-performing sites/locations, adjust the own/partner and in-store/off-site mix, feed learnings to strategy (W4793); manage dependencies with ecommerce (VS-10), facilities (VS-138), and real estate (VS-97)
Responsible (R): Locker Program / PMO / Analytics
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4800_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4800_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4800_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4800_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4800_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-95 (ensure locker network custody &amp; uptime.) | - CTL-722: capex via tiered approval matrix (VS-40); phase-gate review before each release; portfolio reallocation on performance
Owner: Locker Program Manager / PMO (VS-112) / Finance</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
